For most of software history, writing code was the bottleneck.

Today, understanding it is.

AI can generate thousands of lines of code in seconds. Frameworks abstract away complexity. Libraries hide implementation details. Entire applications are assembled from layers of dependencies that most developers never inspect.

We've made software dramatically easier to build.

But we've done almost nothing to make it easier to understand.

And that's becoming a problem.

Every day, developers spend hours answering questions that should take seconds.

What component is rendering this?

Where is this data coming from?

Which API powers this feature?

What third-party scripts are running on this page?

What can actually access user data?

The answers exist. They're just buried beneath layers of abstraction.

So we built Archify.

## Understanding Software Shouldn't Feel Like Archaeology

When you land on an unfamiliar application, your first instinct is usually the same.

Open DevTools.

Inspect elements.

Dig through network requests.

Search through source maps.

Trace API calls.

Jump between documentation, repositories, and browser tabs.

Eventually, you piece together a mental model of what's happening.

The problem isn't that the information is unavailable.

The problem is that understanding requires too much effort.

Modern development tools are excellent at exposing implementation details.

They're much less effective at exposing architecture.

Archify changes that.

## Meet Archify

Archify is a browser extension that reveals what's actually happening behind any web application.

Hover over an element and instantly understand:

• The component rendering it

• The framework or library behind it

• The API connections powering it

• The scripts running on the page

• The relationships between different parts of the system

Instead of spending hours tracing behavior through browser tabs and source files, you get immediate visibility into the architecture itself.

Not just what exists.

But how everything fits together.

## Built for Understanding, Not Surveillance

Most developer tools today start with the assumption that your data should leave your machine.

We disagree.

- Archify runs entirely within your browser.
- No cloud processing.
- No server-side analysis.
- No source code uploads.
- No accounts.
- No hidden telemetry.

The systems you're exploring remain yours.

Always.

## Why This Matters

The software industry is entering a new era.

AI is making code generation nearly effortless.

But generated code still needs to be reviewed.

Dependencies still need to be trusted.

Applications still need to be understood.

The ability to build software is accelerating.

The ability to comprehend software isn't.

That gap is growing every day.

We believe the next generation of developer tools won't be defined by how much code they can generate.

They'll be defined by how quickly they can help people understand what already exists.

That's the future Archify is building toward.

A future where understanding software is as fast as interacting with it.

